@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Orange is an XMPP server and a command-line XMPP client for GNU/Linux.
It has three programs and one library:

@table @command
@item oranged
The XMPP server.  Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later.

@item orange-agent
A per-user daemon that keeps the client's XMPP sessions open and serves
them to other programs on a unix socket.

@item orange-cli
Subcommands (@samp{send}, @samp{roster}, @samp{log}, @samp{listen}) and
an interactive mode, all talking to @command{orange-agent}.
@command{orange-agent} and @command{orange-cli} are licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.

@item liborange
The protocol code shared by the server and the client.  Licensed under
the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later.
@end table

@node Building
@chapter Building

Orange needs a C++23 compiler (GCC 14 or later, or Clang 18 or later
with libstdc++ 14), expat, OpenSSL 3, SQLite 3 and standalone asio.
Catch2 3 is needed only to run the unit tests.

From a release tarball:

@example
./configure
make
make check
make install
@end example

From a git checkout, run @command{./autogen.sh} first.  It needs
Autoconf 2.71, Automake 1.16, Libtool and pkg-config (or pkgconf).

@command{configure} accepts these options in addition to the standard
ones:

@table @option
@item --disable-server
Do not build @command{oranged}.

@item --disable-client
Do not build @command{orange-agent} and @command{orange-cli}.

@item --enable-werror
Treat compiler warnings as errors.

@item --enable-sanitizers
Build with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
@end table

@node oranged
@chapter Running the server

@command{oranged} is not implemented yet.  It accepts @option{--help}
and @option{--version}; started without options it reports that and
exits with status 1.  A usage error exits with status 2.

@node orange-agent
@chapter The client session daemon

@command{orange-agent} is not implemented yet.  It will listen on
@file{$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/orange/agent.sock}; started without options it
prints that path and exits with status 1.  If @env{XDG_RUNTIME_DIR} is
unset or not an absolute path, it says so and exits with status 1.

@node orange-cli
@chapter Using XMPP from the command line

@example
orange-cli [@var{option}]@dots{} [@var{command} [@var{argument}]@dots{}]
@end example

Without a command, @command{orange-cli} starts the interactive mode.
The commands are @samp{send}, @samp{roster}, @samp{log}, @samp{listen}
and @samp{repl}.  None of them is implemented yet; each reports that and
exits with status 1.  An unknown command or option exits with status 2.

